//
// **THIS FILE IS NOT IBEX's.  IT IS WRITTEN HERE**, and it is the one file
// under `third_party/ibex/` that is.  Everything else in this directory is
// lowRISC's, byte for byte, under Apache-2.0.
//
// WHAT IT IS FOR.  This repository lints at `-Wall` with warnings fatal, and
// Ibex does not lint clean at that setting: it is written to lowRISC's own
// standard with lowRISC's own waiver file, and `make build/arty_a7.pass` would
// stop on some sixty warnings in code nobody here is going to change.
//
// **AND IBEX's OWN WAIVER IS NOT THE ANSWER, WHICH IS WHY THIS EXISTS.**
// `lint/verilator_waiver.vlt` upstream opens with a bare
// `lint_off -rule PINCONNECTEMPTY` --- no file, no match --- so reading it
// would turn that warning off for THIS PROJECT's files too, silently, for
// ever.  An exemption too wide tests nothing and looks exactly like one that
// is right, which this repository has met often enough to name.  So the
// waivers below are scoped to the vendored directory by file glob and reach
// nothing else, and every file in `rtl/`, `tb/` and `boards/` stays at the
// full standard.
//
// The three rules, and what each is:
//
//   PINCONNECTEMPTY  `.PORT()` written out rather than left off.  That is how
//                    Xilinx's own templates and lowRISC's code are written,
//                    and `boards/arty-z7-20/cadr_arty.sv` turns the same rule
//                    off around its own MMCM for the same reason
//   UNUSEDPARAM      parameters of a configurable core that this
//                    configuration does not reach.  A core with every
//                    parameter used in every configuration would be a core
//                    with no configurations
//   UNUSEDSIGNAL     bits of a signal a generate branch this configuration
//                    does not take would have read
//
// **A FOURTH RULE IS NOT ADDED WITHOUT A SENTENCE HERE SAYING WHAT IT IS.**
// A waiver list that grows by one line at a time is how a lint stops being a
// check, and the way to keep it honest is to make each line cost a paragraph.

`verilator_config

lint_off -rule PINCONNECTEMPTY -file "*third_party/ibex/*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM     -file "*third_party/ibex/*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL    -file "*third_party/ibex/*"
